WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.780
The marine admirals are some of the&nbsp;
strongest characters in all of One Piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.160
with the likes of Garp, Akainu or&nbsp;
Sengoku being more than capable of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.760
fighting even Yonko-Level Pirates:&nbsp;
Which actually makes you wonder:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:17.220
What WOULD happen if the admirals had&nbsp;
actually become pirates instead of marines?

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.920
And we are starting this video at lightspeed with&nbsp;
Admiral Kizaru: or as he’s known in this timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.680
Captain Borsalino. In case you didn’t know,&nbsp;
every admiral has a code name that translates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.900
in japanese to a color and an animal:&nbsp;
Kizaru meaning Yellow Monkey. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.340
since Borsalino never becomes a pirate in&nbsp;
this timeline, he never gets this code name.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:43.740
So, what would this guy be like if not for&nbsp;
the marines? Well, let’s take a look at his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.720
inspiration: Every single admiral is based&nbsp;
on a famous Japanese actor. In this case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.280
Borsalino is based on Kunie Tanaka,&nbsp;
an actor well-known for playing thugs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.920
mobsters, and yakuza members. In addition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.860
his name, “Borsalino” comes from a French movie&nbsp;
called…Borsalino, which is also about a mobster.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:07.320
In fact, just look at this old flashback&nbsp;
version of Borsalino and it’s even easier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.540
to tell that this guy was clearly modeled&nbsp;
on a gangster. Unlike other admirals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.360
he doesn’t go on and on about justice. It seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.580
more like he’s just an enforcer for the most&nbsp;
powerful gang around: the world government.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.400
But let’s say baby Borsalino didn’t want to be&nbsp;
a square, working for “the man” - where would he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:32.160
go? Well, it seems like an organized crime&nbsp;
family would be the perfect place for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:38.040
which would put him right at home on a crew&nbsp;
like Capone Bege’s…Unfortunately the timeline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:43.380
doesn’t work for that since Bege only set sail&nbsp;
as a pirate a few years ago in the story. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:49.500
we do happen to have another great contender&nbsp;
for a mafia family: The Donquixote Family.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.340
That’s right - in this timeline, a young&nbsp;
Borsalino looking for a job where he gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:58.920
free reign to beat people up would cross paths&nbsp;
with none other than the Doflamingo Family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:04.440
Trebol and the other executives would make&nbsp;
him an offer he couldn’t refuse: in just the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.940
same way that the World Government gives Kizaru&nbsp;
free reign to deal with pirates, Doflamingo’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:14.940
status as a Celestial Dragon also grants his&nbsp;
crew a degree of immunity from consequences.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.880
For the sake of argument, we’ll say that somewhere&nbsp;
along the way, Borsalino will still get his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.800
light-light fruit. After all, as underworld&nbsp;
brokers,&nbsp; the Doflamingo family is pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:33.900
good at procuring strong devil fruits. We can even&nbsp;
say that Pica helps him get the Pika-Pika no Mi.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:42.720
However, all this does raise a big concern…How&nbsp;
can Borsalino be a subordinate on Doffy’s crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:49.080
if he’s so much stronger than Doflamingo?&nbsp;
Well, it is a bit out of the ordinary for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.780
crew mate to be stronger than their captain,&nbsp;
but does Borsalino really strike you as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:01.740
ambitious type? He was more than happy to sit&nbsp;
back and relax while Sakazuki and Kuzan fought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:06.300
over the Fleet Admiral position. As long&nbsp;
as he has the power to do what he wants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:11.580
Borsalino seems more than happy to play second&nbsp;
fiddle to someone else and not have to carry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:15.540
all the burdensome responsibilities&nbsp;
that come with being the top dog.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.900
Doflamingo having a powerhouse like Borsalino&nbsp;
working with him would totally alter the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.640
landscape of One Piece. The beginning of&nbsp;
the trajectory looks the same - they would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.440
capture Dressrosa with ease and Doffy would&nbsp;
be named one of the seven warlords. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:36.120
Doflamingo wouldn’t be satisfied stopping&nbsp;
there and working as an arms dealer for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.220
the Yonkou. With the additional power&nbsp;
afforded by Borsalino, he would expand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:47.340
his empire and actually become a Yonkou with&nbsp;
territory on par with Big Mom’s Totto Land.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:52.260
I’d even theorize that with Doflamingo&nbsp;
being pushed against stronger opponents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:56.760
and having stronger subordinates, he&nbsp;
himself would even grow much stronger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:02.040
compared to where we saw him in the series.&nbsp;
Once the Straw Hats arrived on Dressrosa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:07.140
Doffy would have both Borsalino and Fujitora&nbsp;
on his side, allowing him to decimate the Straw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:11.940
Heart alliance. Borsalino would even&nbsp;
take out Sanji with a lightspeed kick.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:19.620
For his status as a Yonkou Commander, Borsalino&nbsp;
earns a bounty of $1 billion berries.However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.400
this bounty doesn’t even compare&nbsp;
to the ones we’ll see later.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:30.780
Fujitora the Purple Tiger - or Issho in&nbsp;
this timeline - is a mysterious guy. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:38.040
he’s clearly a samurai…and where&nbsp;
are samurai from? Wano. And who did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:43.320
we not hear from at all in the&nbsp;
Wano arc? That’s right: Issho.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.040
For the sake of&nbsp; argument, though,&nbsp;
with no other leads to go on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:53.340
we’re going to assume that Issho is from Wano&nbsp;
and it just hasn’t been revealed quite yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.840
After seeing the atrocities committed&nbsp;
by Orochi and Kaidou in his homeland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:03.480
he cut out his own eyes and blinded himself.&nbsp;
He then left Wano to wander the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:09.360
much like the character he’s based on: Zatoichi&nbsp;
the blind samurai portrayed by Shintaro Katsu.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:13.800
However, in this timeline, he first wanders,&nbsp;
directionless. But after finding and eating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:20.520
the gravity fruit, Isshin believes he has gained&nbsp;
enough power to take his country back. He vows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:25.440
to take revenge for his homeland and sets sail&nbsp;
as a pirate. His first step is to find fellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:30.960
allies who are similarly invested in the fight for&nbsp;
Wano. It just so happens that several survivors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:37.140
from Wano were hiding out creating a new life&nbsp;
for themselves in the East Blue. In Shimotsuki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:43.140
Village, most of the citizens fear their ability&nbsp;
to do anything against Kaidou, but Isshin does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:48.360
rally a few people, including a tenacious&nbsp;
young swordsman with his eyes set on becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:55.140
the world’s strongest swordsman. That’s right:&nbsp;
in this timeline, Isshin’s first mate is none&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.140 --> 00:06:02.760
other than Roronoa Zoro, the great nephew of one&nbsp;
of Isshin’s former comrades, Shimotsuki Ushimaru.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:07.800
As the Fujitora we know has a love of gambling,&nbsp;
we think he also wouldn’t be past winning some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:13.200
more powerful crew mates through the pirate&nbsp;
gambling game known as the Davy Back Fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.680
After learning about the game from the&nbsp;
Foxy Pirates and easily defeating them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:22.440
they use this game to recruit more strong&nbsp;
allies to advance on the forces of Wano.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:27.840
Once they finally sail on Wano, Kaidou’s forces&nbsp;
would see a fleet of ships approaching bearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:33.720
an ominous Jolly Roger: a skull crashing&nbsp;
down to Earth like a meteor. The forces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.860
of the beast pirates would be caught&nbsp;
completely off guard as giant meteors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:42.960
crashed down upon Onigashima. The Beast&nbsp;
Pirates would be under siege by Issho,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:48.300
Captain of the&nbsp; Meteor Pirates. Using this as&nbsp;
their opportunity to attack, the Red Scabbards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:54.960
would also come out of hiding to serve as allies&nbsp;
in this sudden war on Kaidou and Orochi’s forces.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:58.980
After a hard-fought battle, a meteor&nbsp;
would plunge Kaidou into the depths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:03.420
beneath Wano to burn in the magma&nbsp;
of Mt. Fuji. For defeating a Yonkou,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:08.460
Isshin would earn a bounty of 3 billion&nbsp;
and be named one of the Four Emperors.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:19.860
Now we need to really stretch our imaginations and&nbsp;
ask the question: What if Kuzan was a pirate??....&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:26.100
Oh wait…he already is a pirate. As the Tenth&nbsp;
Titanic Captain of the Blackbeard Pirates, Admiral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:32.760
Aokiji -or Blue Pheasant -&nbsp; now going by his real&nbsp;
name, Kuzan, is about as pirate as you can get.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:38.460
However, while we’re using our imagination,&nbsp;
let’s write a bit of an alternate history:

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.320
In our imagined timeline, Aokiji doesn’t leave&nbsp;
the marines after his fight with Akainu. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:48.960
he leaves far earlier when his doubts about&nbsp;
whether the marines truly represent justice begin:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:54.480
after the Ohara Incident. After seeing the&nbsp;
innocent civilians of Ohara murdered by Akainu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:59.040
he decides to leave the Marines in order to&nbsp;
seek the truth about what exactly the World&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:05.760
Government was covering up. You see, Kuzan&nbsp;
is based on an actor named Yusaku Matsuda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:10.620
whose most famous role is playing a private eye&nbsp;
in a series called Detective Story - perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.860
fitting for someone who would want&nbsp;
to uncover the truth of the world.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:19.260
Here he rescues his old comrade Saul from his&nbsp;
Ice Time Capsule and together they set sail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:24.120
hiding a young Nico Robin, the sole survivor&nbsp;
of Ohara. Using the resources of Elbaf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:28.380
Saul still rescues the saved books&nbsp;
from Ohara and hides them away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:33.900
and Kuzan and Robin explore the world in&nbsp;
secret collecting poneglyphs in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:40.320
uncover the true history. As Robin grows up, she&nbsp;
becomes officially recognized as his first mate.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:45.060
Kuzan is approached by Monkey D.&nbsp;
Dragon, leader of the Revolutionaries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:50.400
but declines to join forces with them. Theirs&nbsp;
is a journey to seek knowledge, not to make war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.360
against the World Government, however, their&nbsp;
factions are friendly toward one another.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.640
However, there is another up&nbsp;
and coming pirate with a goal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.660
of learning the meaning of the D initial&nbsp;
and what happened during the Void Century:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:09.540
Joining together with Kuzan’s crew as&nbsp;
the ship’s doctor is Trafalgar Law.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:15.780
Due to their low profile and stealthy&nbsp;
operations, the Permafrost Pirates are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:21.300
able to gather the poneglyphs without bringing&nbsp;
too much attention to themselves. Their namesake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:26.100
comes from a combination of Kuzan’s icy abilities&nbsp;
along with permafrost’s association with finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:30.600
well preserved fossils of extinct animals,&nbsp;
fitting for an archaeologist like Robin.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:39.120
Just imagine: a crew where Robin and Law’s&nbsp;
strategic minds can enact plans without Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:44.940
there to completely ruin them instantaneously,&nbsp;
and with the muscle that Kuzan can provide where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:51.840
it’s needed if they do get into a fight.&nbsp;
This crew would probably actually be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:57.660
to attain the One Piece…but later on the video,&nbsp;
they’ll have some serious competition for it.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:02.340
Kuzan’s Jolly Roger would be a shivering&nbsp;
skull, encased in ice. For threatening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:07.560
to reveal the true history, Kuzan&nbsp;
earns a bounty of 5 billion berries.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:15.000
Next up, we have an honorable mention, and it’s&nbsp;
Kuzan’s own mentor: Monkey D. Garp - No, he’s not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:21.120
an admiral, but only because he keeps turning down&nbsp;
the position. Garp AKA the Luffy’s grandpa AKA the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:27.000
Hero of the Marines really just makes sense as a&nbsp;
pirate: I mean, just look at this picture of him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:35.340
as a child - does this little wild boy riding a&nbsp;
tiger feel more like a marine or a pirate to you?

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:41.940
Now, we’re not 100% sure what Garp’s motivations&nbsp;
for joining the marines were in the first place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:47.460
but we do know why he refuses to become an&nbsp;
admiral. Ever since the God Valley incident, he’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:53.610
harbored a hatred for the Celestial Dragons. So in&nbsp;
our new timeline, we’ll take it one step further -&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:58.740
whatever happened at God Valley during the battle&nbsp;
against Rocks alongside Roger didn’t just convince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:04.980
Garp to hate the Celestial Dragons - it convinced&nbsp;
him to turn his back on the marines entirely.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:08.520
After God Valley, we know Roger was&nbsp;
inspired to seek out the poneglyphs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.520
uncover the true history, and&nbsp;
find Laugh Tale. But this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:18.120
he has his best bro Garp traveling right alongside&nbsp;
him as a member of his crew. After Roger’s death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:21.960
unfortunately he wasn’t in the&nbsp;
position to save Ace. In addition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:27.120
his rebellious grandson Luffy might even be&nbsp;
inclined to become a marine in this timeline.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:33.840
But like so many of the Roger Pirates, Garp&nbsp;
would take up residence in a key point of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:38.880
Grand Line, looking for and aiding the&nbsp;
potential Joy Boy. It’s probably not a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:43.620
coincidence that Crocus lived at the very start&nbsp;
of the Grand Line, Rayleigh at the halfway point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:50.400
and both of them helped Luffy on his journey.&nbsp;
So, Roger would wait at Lodestar Island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:54.840
the second to last island of the Grand&nbsp;
Line, waiting for Joy Boy to arrive.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:59.460
For his betrayal of the world government&nbsp;
and aiding the pirate king, Garp would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:03.000
earn a bounty of 5 billion berries.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:11.160
And what about another person from Roger’s era?&nbsp;
Before he was Fleet Admiral, Sengoku must have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:16.920
held the position of Admiral as well, which&nbsp;
makes us ask: What if Sengoku was a pirate?

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:21.240
This one is the absolute wildest in the&nbsp;
lineup because out of every character who’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:27.540
held the position of Admiral, Sengoku&nbsp;
is the least pirate of all. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:33.720
there are a few instances where we see Sengoku’s&nbsp;
faith in the marine organization tested. One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:38.340
of these moments is the death of Rocinante.&nbsp;
Others include the cover up of the Impel Down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:44.640
escape and even the entirety of the Shichibukai&nbsp;
system. Could these be enough to make Sengoku,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:48.000
the quintessential honorable marine, quit, though?

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:53.940
No -&nbsp; but he could pretend to&nbsp;
be a pirate as a SWORD member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:59.220
a la X-Drake. Fooling absolutely no one, Sengoku&nbsp;
would set sail as the Captain of the “Actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:04.980
Pirates.” He would frequent places popular&nbsp;
with pirates in order to gather secret intel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:05.609
for the marines. [It would be really great&nbsp;
if we could get the “How do you do fellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.609 --> 00:13:05.700
kids” meme here but with Sengoku in place of&nbsp;
Steve Buscemi and replace kids with pirates]

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:11.400
But should you call him on his bluff, be&nbsp;
ready to face down against the One-Eyed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:17.340
Buddha - his ancient zoan form, but wearing&nbsp;
an eye patch like a true pirate would. To&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:21.780
help keep his cover, the marines have&nbsp;
given him a very convincing bounty of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:27.840
10,000 berries. Which is absolutely nothing&nbsp;
compared to the last admiral on our list.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:33.540
Back to the current admirals, though, we have&nbsp;
the latest admiral we’ve met in the series:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:38.640
Greenbull, real name: Aramaki, based&nbsp;
on a character from the samurai film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:45.480
Ronin-Gai named…Aramaki. He seems to&nbsp;
use his new position as an admiral to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:50.640
run amok with his powers. He’s a devotee&nbsp;
of Fleet Admiral Akainu and is more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:55.620
happy to use violence to try to subjugate Wano&nbsp;
under the authority of the World Government.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:00.840
Had Aramaki just been a pirate, I could&nbsp;
definitely see him being a pirate like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:07.200
Eustass Kid. He enjoys harming the weak or&nbsp;
the innocent just because he can. Due to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.160
survival of the fittest mentality, he also&nbsp;
might get along well with the Beast Pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:16.260
but we have a feeling that without a zoan fruit,&nbsp;
Kaidou just wouldn’t have him on his crew.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:24.060
Instead, in order to reign Aramaki in,&nbsp;
the government would probably give him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:29.940
a position as a Shichibukai. Much in the way he&nbsp;
was conscripted into the marines as an admiral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:33.780
this way the government would still&nbsp;
get to utilize his power while giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:39.900
him some free reign to commit the acts&nbsp;
of violence he really seems to enjoy.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:44.460
If you’re sailing at sea and happen&nbsp;
to sea a forest coming toward you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:49.800
you should probably turn around: It might&nbsp;
just be the Wildwood Pirates. You can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:55.560
tell for certain by their Jolly Roger: a skull&nbsp;
overgrown with foliage and ivy. Their captain:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.560 --> 00:15:03.000
the Forest Man Aramaki, who had a 1 billion berry&nbsp;
bounty before becoming a Warlord of the Sea.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:06.720
Of course, Aramaki might fit&nbsp;
in better as the subordinate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:10.620
of our next marine turned pirate: Sakazuki.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:15.480
The current Fleet Admiral is an&nbsp;
adherent to Absolute Justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:20.640
He hates pirates with every fiber of his&nbsp;
being and wants nothing more than to live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:26.580
in a world without them. So what could&nbsp;
every convince him to become a pirate?

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:32.400
Well, based on Sakazuki’s childhood picture,&nbsp;
it seems like he had a very difficult and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:38.040
violent past. My guess is that his hatred&nbsp;
of pirates is rooted in his childhood - he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:42.600
probably suffered greatly at the hands&nbsp;
of pirates at some point. But what if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:48.060
he fell into the cycle of violence and crime&nbsp;
instead of trying to rise above it? After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:53.580
his likeness, Bunta Sugawara is known for&nbsp;
playing raw, masculine, violent characters.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:16:03.300
What if Sakazuki became the pirate… to end all&nbsp;
pirates? Many pirates seek the One Piece for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:08.520
wealth, fame, or power…but not Sakazuki.&nbsp;
He wants to find the One Piece with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:15.660
singular aim of destroying it - that way it will&nbsp;
never inspire another pirate to set sail again.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:22.260
And he’d have a good shot at doing&nbsp;
it, too. There’s an SBS quote from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:26.040
Oda that once said that if Akainu&nbsp;
was the protagonist of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:31.260
he’d find One Piece in a year. No need&nbsp;
for a two year timeskip for this guy.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:36.240
But wait! That’s actually a misconception&nbsp;
based on a mistranslation of that quote:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:40.800
what Oda actually said is that with&nbsp;
a protagonist as strong as Akainu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:45.660
he’d finish *writing* One Piece in a year.&nbsp;
Hold on. Isn’t that even crazier? I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:50.880
how much time actually passes throughout a&nbsp;
year of publication time during One Piece?

00:16:55.200 --> 00:17:01.020
The raid on Onigashima was published&nbsp;
over the span of like two real-life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:04.800
years! Would Sakazuki just&nbsp;
sail up on all the emperors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:09.000
claim the Road Poneglyphs, and head&nbsp;
to Laugh Tale all in like a night?

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:14.700
Maybe so, especially if he recruits&nbsp;
similarly ruthless crewmates:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:18.240
we could absolutely see people like Shiryu, Lucci,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:24.120
and Aramaki joining Akainu - people who hide&nbsp;
their bloodlust behind the banner of justice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:32.460
would fit right in with his crew, the Bonsai&nbsp;
Pirates - named for Sakazuki’s favorite hobby.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:38.160
Sakazuki would sail for Laugh Tale, his&nbsp;
ship flying a Jolly Roger bursting from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:42.180
the top like a volcanic eruption -&nbsp;
similar to how any pirate-inhabited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:46.860
islands they passed would look once he was&nbsp;
through with them. For spreading violence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:51.660
carnage, and fear throughout the One Piece&nbsp;
world, Sakazuki would be named a Yonkou,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:59.040
but he would have no interest in the title or&nbsp;
holding any territory: only seeking the One Piece.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:04.800
He would be fated to once again face down&nbsp;
Kuzan, but this time not at Punk Hazard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:10.320
But: at Laugh Tale. One of them fighting to&nbsp;
uncover the true history - the other fighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:15.720
to destroy it forever. But we all know how&nbsp;
this fight would turn out. Sakazuki would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:22.020
prove victorious, earning a 10 billion berry&nbsp;
bounty and the title of the Last Pirate King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:25.620
burning every last remnant of Joyboy’s treasure.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:30.480
Akainu really is an absolute monster - no&nbsp;
wonder Luffy couldn’t do anything to him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:36.000
at Marineford. But I wonder if things would&nbsp;
have been different if Luffy had already had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:41.100
all his haki and Gear 5 powers at Marineford,&nbsp;
which lucky you for, you can find out right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:45.600
now in this video right here. Shanks for&nbsp;
watching, and i see you in the next one.

